{{!
    @template tool_vae/attest_page

    The page "Attester une déclaration", below its heading: the declaration, the supporting pieces (a heading, a sentence,
    the list), then the form, or the notice that it is signed, its history and the way out.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\attest_page. The template holds no logic. The
    sentence is escaped (double braces). Seven keys are HTML (triple braces): declarationhtml, drawn by the template
    tool_vae/attest_declaration; headinghtml, a heading made by the core; listhtml, drawn by the template tool_vae/pieces;
    noticehtml, a notification made by the core; attestationshtml, drawn by the template tool_vae/attestations;
    recoursehtml, a button or a notification made by the core; formhtml, the form of the core ($form->render()).

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * declarationhtml - HTML, the declaration and the warning of its anchor
    * pieces - false, or {headinghtml, intro, listhtml}: the supporting pieces
    * signed - false, or {noticehtml, attestationshtml, recoursehtml (false or HTML)}: the declaration is signed
    * formhtml - false, or HTML: the form

    Example context (json):
    {
        "declarationhtml": "<dl class=\"tool-vae-claim\"><dt>Record</dt><dd>RS5000-C01</dd></dl>",
        "pieces": {"headinghtml": "<h3>Supporting pieces</h3>", "intro": "Read them before you sign.",
            "listhtml": "<p>No piece.</p>"},
        "signed": {"noticehtml": "<div class=\"alert alert-info\">Already attested.</div>",
            "attestationshtml": "<ul class=\"tool-vae-attestations\"><li>Signed.</li></ul>", "recoursehtml": false},
        "formhtml": false
    }
}}
{{{declarationhtml}}}
{{#pieces}}
{{{headinghtml}}}
<p>{{intro}}</p>
{{{listhtml}}}
{{/pieces}}
{{#signed}}
{{{noticehtml}}}
{{{attestationshtml}}}
{{#recoursehtml}}
{{{recoursehtml}}}
{{/recoursehtml}}
{{/signed}}
{{#formhtml}}
{{{formhtml}}}
{{/formhtml}}
